## Exact Target A endpoint

For the plateau-terminalized scaffold,

\[
\zeta=\dim\ker S=|C^\partial|-\operatorname{rank}S,
\qquad
s=\Delta_\Lambda-d_{\rm int}.
\]

A survivor has
\[
g=s-\zeta=\Delta_\Lambda-d_{\rm sc}\ge1.
\]

Target A closes exactly if
\[
\boxed{\zeta\ge s},
\]
equivalently
\[
\boxed{
\operatorname{rank}S
\le d_{\rm int}+|C^\partial|-\Delta_\Lambda.
}
\]

A second valid closure is an actual \(N\)-point unit-separated competitor of diameter
strictly below \(D=D(N)\).

## Binding source/capacity facts

For the genuine source \(A\subset H\), fixed-hull Hall capacity is exact:
\[
|Q|-|N_A(Q)|\le\widehat p_H
\]
for every unit-separated \(Q\subset H\). Do not seek a same-hull witness above that
capacity. A source argument needs a strict diameter certificate or direct transport to
the Schur response.

Section 154 gives an \(O(D)\)-defect Hall shadow for every prescribed triangular-lattice
phase. Section 155 co-embeds the smaller optimum and its inner scaffold in the actual
source hull once the explicit \(\rho=\Omega(D^{3/2})\) threshold holds. The remaining
lemma in that subbranch is two-shadow compatibility; pure image-intersection counting
is insufficient.

## Binding activation no-go results

- Section 152: large local activation rank plus coherent monomer incidence can coexist
  with zero response nullity without global optimality.
- Section 153: along the actual global-minimizer activation sequence, every created
  constraint has multiplier zero in every normalized terminal KKT stress.
- Section 156: all created activation constraints can be independently released in an
  exact affine orthant of triangle-free global minimizers.
- Section 158: the activation rows are relative coloops with a finite direction that
  releases every created unit/diameter pair simultaneously.
- Section 159: a universally locked triangle has a nonnegative stress certificate whose
